---
// ABOUTME: Docs page for Pace on GitHub Copilot: the one-line install, what lands in .github/, the commands, updating.
// ABOUTME: Mirrors the install page's layout and styles; the kit itself is generated under copilot/ in the repo.
import SubPage from '../../layouts/SubPage.astro';
import { DOCS_SIDEBAR } from '../../lib/sidebar-data';

const currentPath = '/docs/copilot';
---

<SubPage
  title="GitHub Copilot · Pace"
  description="Install Pace's engineering skills for GitHub Copilot with one command. Slash commands in Copilot chat, the same rules for the coding agent, and a reviewer agent for pull requests."
  activeNav="docs"
  canonicalPath={currentPath}
  sidebarLabel="Docs"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    {DOCS_SIDEBAR.map((group) => (
      <div class="subpage-sidebar-group">
        <span class="subpage-sidebar-group-title">{group.title}</span>
        <ul class="subpage-sidebar-list">
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={item.href}
                aria-current={item.href === currentPath ? 'page' : undefined}
              >{item.label}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </Fragment>

  <article class="installpage">
    <header class="installpage-header">
      <span class="installpage-eyebrow">Get started</span>
      <h1>Pace for GitHub Copilot</h1>
      <p class="installpage-lede">
        The engineering skills, in the shape GitHub Copilot reads. One command puts them into a repo's <code>.github/</code> folder. From then on <code>/grill-me</code>, <code>/to-prd</code>, <code>/to-issues</code>, <code>/tdd</code> and the rest are slash commands in Copilot chat, the coding agent follows the same rules when it takes an issue, and <code>@reviewer</code> reads pull requests against your standards.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="installpage-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="installpage-toc-label">On this page</span>
      <ol class="installpage-toc-list">
        <li><a href="#install">Install</a></li>
        <li><a href="#files">What lands where</a></li>
        <li><a href="#instructions">The instructions file</a></li>
        <li><a href="#commands">The commands</a></li>
        <li><a href="#coding-agent">The coding agent and the reviewer</a></li>
        <li><a href="#updating">Updating</a></li>
        <li><a href="#verifying">Verifying it worked</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="install">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>From the root of the repo you want Copilot to work in:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/main/copilot/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
      <p>On Windows, or if you prefer npm:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>npx pace-tools copilot</code></pre>
      <p>
        Both add files and never delete yours. A skill, prompt or agent that already exists is kept unless you pass <code>--force</code>. <code>--dry-run</code> shows what would change and writes nothing. Then commit <code>.github/</code>, so the whole team and the coding agent get the same setup.
      </p>
      <div class="installpage-callout">
        <strong>No Claude Code needed.</strong> This path is separate from the marketplace. It needs <code>curl</code> or <code>wget</code> and <code>tar</code>, or Node for the <code>npx</code> form, and a git repository to install into.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="files">
      <h2>What lands where</h2>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>.github/
├── copilot-instructions.md      <span class="installpage-comment"># read on every request: the house rules, short</span>
├── skills/
│   ├── grill-me/SKILL.md        <span class="installpage-comment"># read when a task matches: the full instructions</span>
│   ├── to-prd/SKILL.md
│   ├── to-issues/SKILL.md
│   ├── tdd/SKILL.md
│   └── … 29 more, with their reference files
├── prompts/
│   ├── grill-me.prompt.md       <span class="installpage-comment"># /grill-me in Copilot chat; reads the skill</span>
│   └── … one per skill
└── agents/
    └── reviewer.agent.md        <span class="installpage-comment"># @reviewer: a fresh reading of a pull request</span></code></pre>
      <p>
        Two kinds of file. The instructions file is loaded into every session, so it holds only the rules that apply to everything and stays under a screen. The skills folder holds the long instructions; a task reads only the one it needs, and the prompt files are the slash commands that point at them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="instructions">
      <h2>The instructions file</h2>
      <p>
        Pace adds a block to <code>.github/copilot-instructions.md</code> between <code>&lt;!-- pace:start --&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;!-- pace:end --&gt;</code> markers. If the file already exists, the block is appended after your own text; a later install refreshes only the block. What it says, in short:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>When a task matches a skill in <code>.github/skills/</code>, read that file first and follow it.</li>
        <li>Work one issue at a time, as a thin slice through every layer it touches.</li>
        <li>Test first: a failing test, the smallest change that passes, then tidy. Never edit a test to make it pass.</li>
        <li>Run every check the repo has before saying it is done, and paste the result.</li>
        <li>Ask in chat when unsure. Never force-push, bypass hooks, or delete without being asked.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Path-scoped rules go in <code>.github/instructions/*.instructions.md</code> with an <code>applyTo</code> pattern; Pace leaves that folder to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="commands">
      <h2>The commands</h2>
      <p>Type <code>/</code> in Copilot chat, in agent mode, to see them. The five that make up a feature from idea to shipped:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>/grill-me &lt;a brief&gt;     <span class="installpage-comment"># one question at a time, with a recommended answer, until you agree on what to build</span>
/to-prd                  <span class="installpage-comment"># writes the destination down: problem, stories, decisions, out of scope, modules to touch</span>
/to-issues               <span class="installpage-comment"># slices it into issues that each cut through every layer, marks which can run unattended</span>
/tdd                     <span class="installpage-comment"># red, green, refactor on one issue</span>
/code-review             <span class="installpage-comment"># a second reading of the change</span></code></pre>
      <p>
        Run <code>/setup-engineering-skills</code> once per repo first: it tells the skills where your issues live, which labels you use and where your docs are. The rest of the catalog covers debugging (<code>/diagnose</code>), incidents, documentation, deploy checklists, stacked pull requests (<code>/spec</code>, <code>/implement</code>, <code>/topr</code>), triage and architecture (<code>/improve-codebase-architecture</code>). Every skill is listed in the <a href="/docs/skills">skill catalog</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="installpage-aside">
        One engineering skill is left out: <code>git-guardrails-claude-code</code> installs Claude Code hooks and has no Copilot equivalent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="coding-agent">
      <h2>The coding agent and the reviewer</h2>
      <p>
        Assign an issue to Copilot and the coding agent works it in a GitHub Actions runner and opens a pull request. It reads the same <code>copilot-instructions.md</code> and the same skills, so it tests first and runs the checks like anyone else on the team.
      </p>
      <p>
        <code>@reviewer</code> is a custom agent in <code>.github/agents/</code>. It reads a diff in a fresh context, with the standards in front of it, and returns findings marked P1, P2 or P3 and a verdict: approve, or send back. Use it on the coding agent's pull requests before a person reads them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="updating">
      <h2>Updating</h2>
      <p>Run the install again. New skills are added, the pace block in the instructions file is refreshed, and anything you changed is kept unless you pass <code>--force</code>:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>npx pace-tools copilot           <span class="installpage-comment"># adds what is new, keeps what you edited</span>
npx pace-tools copilot --force   <span class="installpage-comment"># replaces the skills, prompts and agent with the current versions</span></code></pre>
      <p>
        To install from a branch or tag instead of <code>main</code>, set <code>PACE_REF</code> in front of either command.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="verifying">
      <h2>Verifying it worked</h2>
      <p>
        Open the repo in VS Code, open Copilot chat in agent mode and type <code>/grill-me</code>. It should appear in the list and, when run with a brief, start asking questions one at a time. Copilot's file layout moves between releases, so check the paths above against the current Copilot docs if a command does not show up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stuck? Open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues">github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SubPage>

<style>
  .installpage {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .installpage-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .installpage-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .installpage-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .installpage-lede a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-paths {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .installpage-paths {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .installpage-path {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-path:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 88%, var(--color-forest-dim));
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .installpage-path-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-path h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .installpage-path p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-path-cta {
    margin-top: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .installpage-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .installpage-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px var(--spacing-md);
    counter-reset: toc;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li {
    counter-increment: toc;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li::before {
    content: counter(toc, decimal-leading-zero) ' ';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a:hover {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-color: var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .installpage-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .installpage-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section ol,
  .installpage-section ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .installpage-section a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-section a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-section strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .installpage-pre {
    background: oklch(18% 0.015 150);
    color: oklch(92% 0.005 150);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-pre code {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-comment {
    color: oklch(62% 0.04 150);
  }
  .installpage-aside {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-style: italic;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-left: 2px;
  }
  .installpage-aside a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-callout {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-forest);
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-callout strong {
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning {
    background: var(--color-clay-dim);
    border-left-color: var(--color-clay);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning strong {
    color: var(--color-clay-hover);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .installpage-toc-list {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
